      "solution": "import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Solution {\n\n\tpublic static void main(String[] args) {\n\t\tScanner in = new Scanner(System.in);\n\t\tint g = in.nextInt();\n\t\tint e = in.nextInt();\n\t\tJumpQueue jq = new JumpQueue(g);\n\n\t\tin.nextLine();\n\n\t\tfor (int i = 0; i < g; i++) {\n\t\t\tString s = in.nextLine();\n\t\t\tjq.setGroup(s, i);\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tString line = in.nextLine();\n\t\tint len = jq.setEvents(line);\n\t\tif (len != e) {\n\t\t\tSystem.err.printf(\"Event count %d not match e\\n\", len);\n\t\t}\n\t\tjq.ans();\n\t}\n}\n\nclass JumpQueue {\n\tint t; // number of groups\n\tList<Queue<Integer>> listOfQueue = new ArrayList<>();\n\tMap<Integer, Integer> map = new HashMap<>(); // groupID : value\n\tList<Integer> idList = new ArrayList<>();\n\tStringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n\n\tpublic JumpQueue(int t) {\n\t\tthis.t = t;\n\t}\n\n\tpublic void ans() {\n\t\tSystem.out.println(sb);\n\t}\n\n\tpublic int setEvents(String line) {\n\t\tString[] ss = line.split(\"\\\\s+\");\n\t\tfor (String s : ss) {\n\t\t\tint v = Integer.parseInt(s);\n\t\t\tif (v == -1) {\n\t\t\t\tdequeue();\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\tenqueue(v);\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn ss.length;\n\t}\n\n\tpublic void dequeue() {\n\t\tfor (Queue<Integer> team : listOfQueue) {\n\t\t\tif (!team.isEmpty()) {\n\t\t\t\tint v = team.poll();\n\t\t\t\tsb.append(v).append(\"\\n\");\n\n\t\t\t\tif (team.isEmpty()) {\n\t\t\t\t\tlistOfQueue.remove(0);\n\t\t\t\t\tidList.remove(0);\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tbreak;\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tpublic void enqueue(int v) {\n\t\tInteger id = map.get(v);\n\n\t\tif (id == null) {\n\t\t\tmap.put(v, t);\n\t\t\tid = t;\n\t\t\tt++;\n\n\t\t\t// lonely wolf join queue at the tail\n\t\t\tQueue<Integer> team = new LinkedList<>();\n\t\t\tteam.add(v);\n\t\t\tlistOfQueue.add(team);\n\t\t\tidList.add(id);\n\n\t\t\treturn;\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tboolean found = false;\n\t\tfor (int i = 0; i < idList.size(); i++) {\n\t\t\tif (idList.get(i) == id) {\n\t\t\t\tfound = true;\n\t\t\t\tQueue<Integer> team = listOfQueue.get(i);\n\t\t\t\tteam.add(v);\n\t\t\t\tbreak;\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif (!found) {\n\t\t\tQueue<Integer> team = new LinkedList<>();\n\t\t\tteam.add(v);\n\t\t\tlistOfQueue.add(team);\n\t\t\tidList.add(id);\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tpublic void setGroup(String s, int id) {\n\t\tString[] ss = s.split(\"\\\\s+\");\n\n\t\tfor (int i = 0; i < ss.length; i++) {\n\t\t\tint v = Integer.parseInt(ss[i]);\n\t\t\tmap.put(v, id);\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n",
      "statement": "A school of students is queueing in line in the school canteen to buy lunchboxes.\nThere is only one counter serving one queue.\n\nWhen a student comes and wants to join the queue, he will search the queue from head to tail to check if any of his friends are already in the queue. If any friend were found, he would jump the queue to insert himself right behind his friend group in the queue. If no friend were found, he would join the queue at the tail.\n\nAssume all students are joining the queue in this manner. Write a program to simulate the working of this queue.",
